# AIM4 control UI style

Use this when designing or restyling filters, toolbars, switches, dropdowns, or side panels on aim4.io (Charts, Database, Analyzer, Timeline, and new tools).

## Do not

- **Descriptive / marketing text is terrible.** Do not put captions, taglines, or “this section does X” copy under headings or next to controls. A control’s own label or placeholder is enough. (Same spirit as `CLAUDE.md` content rules.)
- **Too many labels is terrible.** Prefer text inside the control (`Map`, `Own buy`, `Y Axis`, placeholder search) over uppercase section labels above every row. Drop redundant labels like a lone `TEAM` above a team switch. Use `aria-label` when the visible label is removed.
- **1px outlines on fields/dropdowns are terrible.** Flat filled fields, no border. Do not wrap every input in a hairline box.
- **Do not invent a third control palette.** Reuse the field theme and the analyzer switch theme below.

Em dashes are still banned in UI copy (`CLAUDE.md`).

## Color tokens (site)

From `src/site/site.css`:

| Token | Value | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `--surface` | `#0c0c0c` | Panel / bar chrome |
| `--text` | `#f2f2f2` | Selected / primary action text |
| `--muted` | `#9c9ca2` | Inactive switch / button text |
| `--border` | `#181818` | Switch outer edge + segment splits |
| `--radius` | `12px` | Large panels |
| `--radius-sm` | `8px` | Fields / dropdowns (preferred for inputs) |
| Control radius (switches) | `6px` | Analyzer segs / action buttons |

## Fields and dropdowns

Selects, text inputs, multi-select summaries, min-rounds, clocks, search:

- Background: `#050505`
- Text: `#5c5c62`, **regular** weight (`400`), not light
- Placeholder: same gray / weight
- **No** 1px border, **no** focus ring border
- Height: `32px`
- Border radius: `var(--radius-sm)` (`8px`)
- Custom chevron centered vertically (not floated high). Native `appearance: none` + SVG or `clip-path` caret.

Reference: `.ch-side .site-select` / `.st-filters .site-select` in `src/replays/replays.css`.

## Switches (2+ choices) and buttons

Match the **analyzer** segmented control (`.rv-az-seg` / `.rv-az-seg-btn`):

**Container (seg)**

- `border: 1px solid var(--border)`
- `border-radius: 6px`
- `background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03)`

**Segment / button**

- Idle: transparent (or same faint fill), `color: var(--muted)`, font weight `600`
- Hover: `background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)`, `color: var(--text)`
- Active / on: `background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)`, `color: var(--text)`, `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12)`
- Keep a **1px split** between segments (`border-right: 1px solid var(--border)`), not a second outer outline on each half

Apply this theme to: T/CT, W/L, 5v4/4v5, half, team pickers, AWP toggles, Clear, gear, calendar icon buttons, full-width on/off rows (e.g. “Divide by played rounds”), and compare map/game chips when they act as toggles.

Reference: `.rv-az-seg` in `src/replays/replays.css`; Charts/Database overrides under `.ch-side` and `.st-filters`.

## Layout habits

- Shared control height (`32px`) across a toolbar or sidebar row
- Tight vertical gaps between stacked builder rows; one separator before a real section (e.g. “General filters”), not a line under every block
- Buy dropdowns flex; compact AWP beside them; axis selects fill width minus a square gear
- Prefer one job per row; do not add helper sentences under controls

## Content

- Functional hints (keybinds, editor tooltips) can stay; they still must not use em dashes
- Section titles like “General filters” are OK once per block; do not label every filter “MAP”, “SIDE”, “ROLE” above the control
